;; Pairs of units: a first unit, and a second unit that uses it, checked
;; against the Rocq semantics of Flambda 2 with the .cmx of the first at
;; hand for the tool's Simplify (see README.md).
;;
;; A unit X.ml here is the second unit of a pair if another unit F.ml is
;; here and X is F followed by an underscore and more: F is then its first
;; unit. As in the directory above, X.fl is the term that the compiler gives
;; to Simplify and X.expected is what the test tool prints of it, and both
;; are kept. The rules, which gen_rules.sh writes from the files that are
;; here, compile each unit, a second unit against the .cmi and the .cmx of
;; its first, make X.fl again and compare, and run the tool on X.fl with the
;; directory of the .cmx as its load path and compare. `dune promote`
;; updates either. A unit with no X.expected is compiled and its term
;; compared; the tool is not run on it.
;;
;; To add a pair, add F.ml and F_more.ml, with their .fl and .expected, and
;; nothing else. The rules are included by run/dune and not by this file.

(rule
 (deps
  (glob_files *.ml)
  (glob_files *.fl)
  (glob_files *.expected))
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   dune.inc
   (run sh %{dep:gen_rules.sh} %{deps}))))
